        "format_version": "0.5.10",
        "type": "model",
        "name": "NAFNet-GAN Poisson-Gaussian Microscopy Denoiser",
        "description": "NAFNet-GAN is a supervised denoising model for 2D fluorescence microscopy images affected by realistic Poisson-Gaussian noise. It was developed for the AI4Life Microscopy Supervised Denoising Challenge 2025 and presented at ISBI 2026. The model was trained on the Poisson-Gaussian microscopy dataset, which includes confocal, two-photon, and widefield images from diverse biological samples. It uses a NAFNet-based adversarial framework to reduce noise while preserving fine image structures and the original input intensity range.",
        "authors": [
            {
                "name": "Guillermo Rey-Paniagua",
                "affiliation": "Universidad Carlos III de Madrid, Getafe, Madrid, Spain",
                "orcid": "0009-0001-1903-2892"
